          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#ViaTheDoldKanCorrespondence Via the Dold-Kan correspondence
          %p
            When the coefficient object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            is “sufficiently abelian” in that under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            it is represented by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            then using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidalness
            of the Dold-Kan correspondence (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} monoidal Dold-Kan correspondence
          %p Write
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Ch
                        %mrow
                          %mo •
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ch_{\bullet \geq 0}, \otimes)
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
                with the standard
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi sAb
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (sAb, \otimes)
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+abelian+groups"} simplicial abelian groups
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
                with the degreewise
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of abelian groups
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi sAb
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi KanCplx
                      %mo →
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \;\colon\; sAb \longrightarrow KanCplx \to sSet
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
                to the underlying
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
                (which happens to land in
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi Ch
                        %mrow
                          %mo •
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 0
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ≃
                      %mi sAb
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \;\colon \; Ch_{\bullet \geq 0} \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} sAb
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
                given by the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi DK
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi Ch
                        %mrow
                          %mo •
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 0
                      %munderover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi Γ
                      %mi sAb
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi F
                      %mi KanCplx
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DK \;\colon\; Ch_{\bullet \geq 0} \underoverset{\simeq}{\Gamma}{\longrightarrow} sAb \stackrel{F}{\longrightarrow} KanCplx \hookrightarrow sSet
                for the composite.
          %p Now:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi γ
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
